  "result": "Excellent! The CSV export feature has been successfully implemented. Here's what was added:\n\n**src/export.js** \u2014 New `exportCsv(invoices)` function that:\n- Returns a CSV-formatted string with header and data rows\n- Header: `number,customer,issueDate,dueDate,status,subtotal,discount,vat,total,due`\n- One data line per invoice in the order given\n- Customer field uses the customer's name (not ID)\n- Amounts formatted as plain euros: 2 decimal places, dot separator, no \u20ac, no thousands separator (e.g., 1234.50)\n- Proper CSV escaping:\n  - Fields with commas or quotes are wrapped in double quotes\n  - Internal double quotes are doubled (e.g., `\"Company \"\"ABC\"\" Inc\"`)\n- Each line (including header) ends with `\\n`\n\n**test/export.test.js** \u2014 21 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Empty invoice list (header only)\n- Header line format and presence\n- Proper line ending with \\n\n- Single and multiple invoices\n- All 10 required columns\n- Amount formatting (no \u20ac sign, no thousands separators, 2 decimals)\n- Customer name usage\n- CSV field quoting for commas\n- CSV field quoting for internal quotes (doubling)\n- Multiple invoices in given order\n- Correct totals calculation\n- Invoice status display\n- Due amounts for unpaid, partially paid, and fully paid invoices\n- Large amounts formatting\n- Valid CSV parsing\n- Trailing newline\n\n**All 269 tests pass** \u2713",
